{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QaZJBGngMR54F2pdYfPxKJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Trust\n2\t\n3\t`src/config/trust.ts`, `src/config/canonical.ts`, `src/trust/trust.ts`,\n4\t`src/cli/trust.ts`. Design: ADR-0001, ADR-0003. How CLI tests approve a\n5\tconfig is in `typescript.md`.\n6\t\n7\t- `trustProjection(cfg)` is the security-relevant projection; its\n8\t  `trustHash` covers only endpoint, protocol, credential variable, and\n9\t  prompt-override paths. A new security-relevant config field goes into\n10\t  the projection, or it can change without re-approval.\n11\t- Approvals live in `<git-common-dir>/roast/trust.json`. `roast review`\n12\t  calls `requireTrust` before building scope; untrusted is a usage error\n13\t  (exit 2), never the findings exit.\n14\t- `src/config/trust.ts` (projection, `requiresApproval`, hash v2) is\n15\t  pure. `src/config/canonical.ts` is the only JSON canonicalizer; its\n16\t  input types must be `type` aliases, not interfaces, to be assignable\n17\t  to `CanonicalValue`.\n18\t- `src/trust/trust.ts` takes a trailing `{signal, env}` for git.\n19\t  `src/cli/trust.ts` has the command, `writeTrustSummary` (every value\n20\t  through `textsafe.line`) and `requireTrust(dir, cfg, io)`.\n21\t  `promptNoDefault` (`[y/N]`) lives in `src/cli/terminal.ts`.\n22\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01D3vMhfKEa3y1FeL1F2HcCq","agent_id":"a85f2eb3553f193db","session_id":"fa31655d-debc-49e9-83c6-d8bc618478fe","uuid":"ea4e9005-6b25-45c3-ba44-f397fb55c433","timestamp":"2026-11-24T22:23:51.665Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QaZJBGngMR54F2pdYfPxKJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"fork","task_description":"Read all relevant source files"}
