{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a85f2eb3553f193db","run_id":"0mwv9hg0c-682ce5e5","tool_use_id":"toolu_01D3vMhfKEa3y1FeL1F2HcCq","status":"completed","output_file":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-nick-code-roast-init-model-prompts-03-custom-endpoint-choice/fa31655d-debc-49e9-83c6-d8bc618478fe/tasks/a85f2eb3553f193db.output","summary":"Now I have a thorough understanding of the codebase. Here's my report:\n\n---\n\n## File Contents Report\n\n### 1. `docs/agents/config.md`\nFull config area notes (103 lines). Key points:\n- `loadConfig(path)` parses `.roast.json` as JSONC\n- `starter()` takes a `RoleChoice` per role (provider + model). `starterFromModels()` is backward-compat wrapper\n- `choiceFromModel()` builds a `RoleChoice` from a flag value\n- `placeModel` places a model by its ID alone\n- `SUGGESTED_MODELS` in `defaults.ts`\n- Interactive prompt flow in `src/cli/init.ts`: `promptRoleChoice` per role, calling `promptProvider` then `promptModel`\n- Menu order hardcoded in `PROVIDER_MENU` (Anthropic, OpenAI, OpenRouter)\n\n### 2. `docs/agents/typescript.md`  \nFull typescript notes (147 lines). Key points:\n- `npm test` builds then bundles and runs tapzero suite; doesn't typecheck\n- `npm run test:one -- test/<area>/<file>.ts` bundles one test module\n- Use `test` wrapper from `test/helpers/test.ts` with `t.cleanup`\n- CLI tests use `runRoast` from `test/helpers/run.ts`, `tempRepo` from `test/helpers/repo.ts`\n- `isolatedEnv` strips all `ROAST_*`, `OPENAI_*`, `OPENROUTER_*`, `ANTHROPIC_*` vars\n- `simulateTerminals` / `captureBrowser` from `test/helpers/terminal.ts`\n\n### 3. `docs/agents/trust.md`\nTrust area notes (22 lines). Key points:\n- `trustProjection(cfg)` is security-relevant projection; `trustHash` covers endpoint, protocol, credential variable, prompt-override paths\n- `requiresApproval` checks if any profile is non-standard\n- `writeTrustSummary` and `promptNoDefault` (`[y/N]`) in `src/cli/terminal.ts`\n\n### 4. `src/cli/init.ts` (385 lines)\nFull init command. Key structures:\n- `PROVIDER_MENU` = [{num:'1', name:'anthropic'}, {num:'2', name:'openai'}, {num:'3', name:'openrouter'}]\n- `suggestedModel(provider, otherChoice)` - picks suggested model for a provider\n- `defaultProvider(role, otherChoice)` - finder defaults to 'openai', verifier uses `otherProvider`\n- `parseProviderInput(input)` - parses number or name\n- `promptProvider(out, lines, role, otherChoice)` - shows numbered menu, loops on invalid\n- `promptModel(out, lines, role, provider, otherChoice)` - shows suggested, validates via `placeModel`\n- `promptRoleChoice(out, lines, role, otherChoice)` - calls promptProvider then promptModel, returns `RoleChoice|null`\n- `writeStarterFromChoices(cwd, finder, verifier)` - writes starter using `starter()` function\n- `writeStarter(cwd, finderModel, verifierModel)` - writes starter using `starterFromModels()` (flag path)\n- `offerLogin(file, ctx)` - loads config, finds providers needing login, offers each\n- Handler: checks git root, checks no existing config, determines interactive, prompts per role, writes config, ignores state, offers login\n\n### 5. `src/config/starter.ts` (187 lines)\nFull starter module. Key structures:\n- `RoleChoice` = `{readonly provider:string; readonly model:string}`\n- `TEMPLATE` - the JSONC template with `__PROFILES__`, `__FINDER_PROFILE__`, `__VERIFIER_PROFILE__` placeholders\n- `placeModel(model)` - places model onto provider by ID pattern analysis. Returns provider name or null\n- `UnplaceableModelError` - thrown when model can't be placed\n- `otherProvider(provider)` - openrouter->openrouter, openai<->anthropic\n- `starterProfile(name, provider, model)` - renders one profile block using `lookupProvider(provider)!`\n- `starter(finder, verifier)` - renders full config. Split logic: same provider, different models = `-finder`/`-verifier` suffix\n- `choiceFromModel(role, model, otherChoice)` - builds RoleChoice from flag\n- `starterFromModels(finderModel, verifierModel)` - backward compat wrapper\n\n### 6. `src/config/defaults.ts` (38 lines)\nShared defaults. Contains `SUGGESTED_MODELS` with anthropic, openai, and openrouter entries.\n\n### 7. `src/config/endpoint.ts` (41 lines)\n- `PROTOCOLS` = ['chat', 'responses', 'anthropic']\n- `isProtocol(p)` - type guard\n- `endpointProblem(field, endpoint, protocol, maxOutputTokens)` - validates endpoint URL using `parseEndpoint`\n\n### 8. `src/config/credential.ts` (242 lines)\n- `roleKeyVar(role)` = `ROAST_${role.toUpperCase()}_API_KEY`\n- `envValue(env, name)` - reads env var\n- `resolveCredential(roleName, apiKeyEnv, role, env)` - resolves credential from role var, profile var, ambient\n- `storedCredential` - only for builtin providers; custom endpoints never get stored keys\n- `ambientCredential` - builtin provider's standard key or stored key\n\n### 9. `src/config/provider.ts` (133 lines)\n- `REGISTRY` - 3 builtin providers: openai (responses, chat), anthropic (anthropic), openrouter (chat, responses)\n- `lookupProvider(name)` - by exact name\n- `providerAt(endpoint, protocol)` - provider that accepts protocol at endpoint\n- `parseEndpoint(s)` - URL parser\n- `sameEndpoint(a, b)` - endpoint comparison\n\n### 10. `test/cli/init.ts` (561 lines total)\nTests for init command. Structure:\n- `initLoginRepo(t, terminals)` helper: creates temp repo, provider server, simulated terminals, returns `{repo, server, opened, project, user, run}`\n- Existing tests cover: reject existing config, unplaceable models, write usable settings, placeholders, schema ref, login offers, declining providers, --no-login, failed keys, skips when creds exist\n- Ticket 02 tests (lines 261-561): prompt by number, prompt by name, verifier default, --finder-model only, both flags, no terminals, invalid menu choice, model mismatch, EOF, existing config rejection, same-model note, login after prompts\n\n### 11. `test/config/starter.ts` (215 lines total)\nTests for starter module. Structure:\n- Tests `starterFromModels` with many model combinations\n- Profile naming tests\n- Unplaceable ID rejection tests\n- Suggested model constant tests\n- `RoleChoice` acceptance test\n- Comment/default agreement tests\n\n### 12. `src/cli/trust.ts` (143 lines)\nTrust command and `requireTrust`. Key functions:\n- `writeTrustSummary(out, projection)` - prints all security-relevant values\n- `requireTrust(dir, cfg, io)` - checks approval, asks on interactive terminals\n- `promptNoDefault` used for trust question with `[y/N]` default\n\n### 13. `src/cli/terminal.ts` (231 lines)\n- `LineReader` class with `readLine()` and `readChar()`\n- `promptYesDefault` - `[Y/n]`, default yes\n- `promptNoDefault` - `[y/N]`, default no\n- `readSecret` - raw mode on TTY\n- `interactiveTerminals` - swappable via `terminalHooks`\n\n### 14. `src/config/trust.ts` (138 lines)\n- `trustProjection(cfg)` - builds TrustProjection with profiles and prompt overrides\n- `requiresApproval(p)` - true if any profile is non-standard (not on builtin provider's endpoint with its standard key)\n- `trustHash(p)` - sha256 hash of canonical JSON of hash document\n\n### 15. `src/config/role.ts` (first 80 lines)\n- `resolveRole(cfg, name, env)` - expands a configured role into ResolvedRole\n- `resolveProfile` - resolves a profile including credential","usage":{"total_tokens":83449,"tool_uses":18,"duration_ms":79519},"uuid":"35a4b875-a86f-459f-9318-cb935a83a1f6","session_id":"fa31655d-debc-49e9-83c6-d8bc618478fe"}
