ge, then regenerates; never edit the JSON by hand.\n  `test/config/schema.ts` fails on drift. Editor-only constraints (enum,\n  pattern, minimum, required) go in the zod `.meta()`.\n- The `roast init` starter (`starter.ts`) shows commented-out defaults\n  from `defaults.ts`, the same module runtime settings use.\n- `starter()` takes a `RoleChoice` per role (provider + model).\n  `starterFromModels()` is the backward-compat wrapper that maps model\n  strings onto choices via `placeModel` / `otherProvider`.\n  `choiceFromModel()` builds a `RoleChoice` from a flag value.\n- `placeModel` places a model by its ID alone: a\n  `<vendor>/<model>[:<variant>]` ID goes to OpenRouter, a bare ID to the\n  provider `inferFamily` names. A placeholder role follows an OpenRouter\n  role onto OpenRouter; otherwise it takes the other direct provider.\n- Suggested model IDs for each built-in provider live in\n  `SUGGESTED_MODELS` (`defaults.ts`). The `UnplaceableModelError`\n  example text uses them so the two cannot drift.\n- Interactive prompt flow lives in `src/cli/init.ts`:\n  `promptRoleChoice` per role, calling `promptProvider` then\n  `promptModel`. The menu order is hardcoded in `PROVIDER_MENU`\n  (Anthropic, OpenAI, OpenRouter). `suggestedModel()` picks the\n  default from `SUGGESTED_MODELS`; for OpenRouter, it picks the\n  slug for the vendor the other role is not using. A typed model at\n  a built-in provider must pass `placeModel` and land on the chosen\n  provider.\n\n## Providers\n\n- `lookupProvider(name)` and `providerAt(endpoint, protocol)`\n  (`provider.ts`) are the one place that says which endpoint,\n  protocols, standard key variable, key page, and login method a\n  provider has. Trust standardness, ambient credentials, and the `init`\n  starter consult it; add a provider there, not in those callers. A\n  provider's first protocol is the one starter profiles use.\n- A new provider's key variable must be stripped from test\n  environments: see `cleanEnv` in `typescript.md`.\n- `defaultBaseURL(protocol)` stays separate: it is the implicit endpoint\n  of a profile that omits one; OpenRouter is never one.\n- A role that gets no ambient key reports any set provider key variable\n  as withheld (`withheldKey`, `credential.ts`), preferring the\n  protocol's default provider.\n- `parseEndpoint` (`provider.ts`) is the one endpoint parser (treats\n  `https:///v1` and `https:v1` as an empty host); `endpoint.ts` and\n  `sameEndpoint` use it.\n\n## Roles (`role.ts`, `credential.ts`, `provider.ts`)\n\n- Resolution takes `env` explicitly and never reads `process.env`.\n- `ResolvedRole` is frozen with a non-enumerable `apiKey` and `stored`,\n  so JSON, spread, and `util.inspect` omit the secret. Change a role\n  with `updateRole(role, changes)`; a `{...role}` spread drops the key.\n- `StoredCredentials` lives in `credential.ts` (re-exported by\n  `load.ts`).\n\n## Tests\n\n- Role tests build configs with `configFrom` / `resolveFinder` and the\n  in-memory `FakeStore` in `test/config/helpers.ts`.\n- Configs the tests load as realistic examples go in\n  `test/config/examples.ts`; the schema test validates each with ajv.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":46,"oldLines":25,"newStart":46,"newLines":39,"lines":["   pattern, minimum, required) go in the zod `.meta()`."," - The `roast init` starter (`starter.ts`) shows commented-out defaults","   from `defaults.ts`, the same module runtime settings use.","-- `starter()` takes a `RoleChoice` per role (provider + model).","+- `starter()` takes a `StarterChoice` per role -- either a `RoleChoice`","+  (provider + model) for built-in providers or a `CustomChoice`","+  (endpoint, protocol, apiKeyEnv, model) for custom endpoints.","   `starterFromModels()` is the backward-compat wrapper that maps model","   strings onto choices via `placeModel` / `otherProvider`.","   `choiceFromModel()` builds a `RoleChoice` from a flag value."," - `placeModel` places a model by its ID alone: a","   `<vendor>/<model>[:<variant>]` ID goes to OpenRouter, a bare ID to the","-  provider `inferFamily` names. A placeholder role follows an OpenRouter","-  role onto OpenRouter; otherwise it takes the other direct provider.","+  provider `inferFamily` names. Custom model IDs skip `placeModel`","+  entirely -- they stay on whatever custom endpoint the user typed. A","+  placeholder role follows an OpenRouter role onto OpenRouter; otherwise","+  it takes the other direct provider.","+- Custom profile naming: a single custom role uses `custom`; when both","+  roles are custom with different settings or models, they split to","+  `custom-finder` and `custom-verifier`; identical settings share","+  `custom`."," - Suggested model IDs for each built-in provider live in","   `SUGGESTED_MODELS` (`defaults.ts`). The `UnplaceableModelError`","   example text uses them so the two cannot drift."," - Interactive prompt flow lives in `src/cli/init.ts`:","   `promptRoleChoice` per role, calling `promptProvider` then","-  `promptModel`. The menu order is hardcoded in `PROVIDER_MENU`","-  (Anthropic, OpenAI, OpenRouter). `suggestedModel()` picks the","-  default from `SUGGESTED_MODELS`; for OpenRouter, it picks the","-  slug for the vendor the other role is not using. A typed model at","-  a built-in provider must pass `placeModel` and land on the chosen","-  provider.","+  `promptModel` (built-in) or `promptCustomEndpoint` (custom). The","+  menu order is hardcoded in `PROVIDER_MENU` (Anthropic, OpenAI,","+  OpenRouter, Custom endpoint). `suggestedModel()` picks the default","+  from `SUGGESTED_MODELS`; for OpenRouter, it picks the slug for the","+  vendor the other role is not using. A typed model at a built-in","+  provider must pass `placeModel` and land on the chosen provider.","+- When the finder chooses Custom, the verifier's default provider is","+  also Custom, and its endpoint, protocol, and key variable prompts","+  default to the finder's answers.","+- After writing a config with custom endpoints, `init` offers trust","+  approval (using `writeTrustSummary` and `promptNoDefault`) and prints","+  a credential hint naming the variable to export."," "," ## Providers"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GtnMmxnjubezEizrQEWcgw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
